{
  "description": "Which checkpoint format holds what (#275, ADR-0024, ADR-0029), written by hand. approval.request and principal are each present exactly on the versions that say so: principal on 4 and 6, approval.request on 5 and 6. So dropping either from a checkpoint that has it is refused on read, and neither can be added to a version that does not name it. Published checkpoint 3 is frozen and a run that keeps no text stays at the version it was. items are the two new formats. cases are reader inputs: the version, whether approval.request is there, whether principal is there, and whether it reads. A release before these versions refuses them (run at the v0.12.0 tag). go/context/durable_writes_test.go and storage/durableWrites.test.ts read every case, and tests/test_contract.py derives each from the rule.",
